                  <provenance type="#em"><orgName role="fmo" key="mlgbOrg_198">Eton,
                        Buckinghamshire. Royal College of the Assumption of Saint Mary the Virgin.
                        </orgName><p>'Liber magistri Iohannis Mocer vicarii de tenterden emptus
                        cantuarie a executoribus magistri Thome maris et a magistro Simone hogges
                        officiali pro xxxiii s. iiij d.'. Thomas Mareys, rector of Sturmouth in
                        Kent, d. 1472. Bequeathed to Eton with three others (MS 106 also survives)
                        by John Mower, vicar of Tenterden in Kent in 1489 (see Willoughby,
                        Collegiate Churches, SC233).</p><p>The manuscript also contains the
                        marginalia of Robert Elyot, fellow of Eton from c. 1474 until his death in
                        January 1499 (BRUO 638). He was a prolific annotator of books at Eton. Five
                        are particularly heavily marked and were probably his own, subsequently
                        given to the college: MSS 17, 18, 34, 36, 76. (His marks were discussed by
                        N. R. Ker in The Library, 5th ser. 30 (1975), 233--7, with an addendum by R.
                        Beadle in The Library, 5th ser. 32 (1977), 371--2.)</p></provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">An earlier inscription records purchase by Mr
                     Thomas Mareys, rector of Stourmouth (Kent) from the executors of Mr Thomas
                     Chichele, archdeacon of Canterbury, 30 April 1468.</provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">John Mower (d. 1489), by whom given to
                     Eton.</provenance>
               </history>
